<article class="env-lemma" id="09TP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09TP">Lemma <span data-tag="09TP">77.9.3</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/083F" data-tag="083F">77.7.1</a>. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$f$ is locally of finite presentation, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathcal{G}$ is of finite type, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the support of $\mathcal{G}$ is proper over $B$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $F_{surj}$ is an algebraic space and $F_{surj} \to B$ is an open immersion. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Consider $\mathop{\mathrm{Coker}}(u)$. Observe that $\mathop{\mathrm{Coker}}(u_ T) = \mathop{\mathrm{Coker}}(u)_ T$ for any $T/B$. Note that formation of the support of a finite type quasi-coherent module commutes with pullback (Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/07TY" data-tag="07TY">67.15.1</a>). Hence $F_{surj}$ is representable by the open subspace of $B$ corresponding to the open set 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  |B| \setminus |f|(\text{Supp}(\mathop{\mathrm{Coker}}(u)))  \]
</div>
    <p>
       see Properties of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/03BZ" data-tag="03BZ">66.4.8</a>. This is an open because $|f|$ is closed on $\text{Supp}(\mathcal{G})$ and $\text{Supp}(\mathop{\mathrm{Coker}}(u))$ is a closed subset of $\text{Supp}(\mathcal{G})$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>